1
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:06,540
Do you realize this is the last time we'll be here in the coffeehouse...

2
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:08,340
...as six single people?

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,510
What's happening to the coffeehouse?

4
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:13,510
Oh! Okay.

5
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:18,720
From now on, it's you four and me and the missus.

6
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:22,470
The little woman. The wife. The old ball and chain.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,980
- Old?     - The young, hot ball and chain.

8
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:28,730
- Much better.     - We gotta go.

9
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,480
- Where?     - Get the dress and lunch with mom.

10
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:34,950
Joey, you too?

11
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,360
I just heard "lunch."

12
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:39,870
Yeah, I can go. Sure.

13
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:46,460
Actually, I'm glad they're leaving.

14
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:49,250
I need to talk to you about something.

15
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:52,590
- What's up?      - This may be a little awkward.

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:57,630
If you need money, it's a bad time. I'm buying dinner for 128 people tomorrow.

17
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,100
No, it's not that.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,430
I'm not gonna say this as your friend...

19
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,060
...but as Monica's older brother.

20
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:10,730
- But you're still my friend?     - Not for a few minutes.

21
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:15,110
- Right now, are you still my best man?     - No.

22
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:19,070
- Do I still call you Ross?      - Okay.

23
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:26,410
You guys are getting married, and I couldn't be more thrilled.

24
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:30,380
But as Monica's older brother, I have to tell you this:

25
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:35,760
If you ever hurt my little sister...

26
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:41,640
...if you ever cause her any unhappiness of any kind...

27
00:01:42,010 --> 00:01:44,100
...I will hunt you down...

28
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:47,020
...and kick your ass.

29
00:01:53,730 --> 00:01:56,400
What? I'm serious.

30
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:03,410
- Dude! Stop it! I'm not kidding.     - I hear what you're saying...

31
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,330
...and thanks for the warning.

32
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,870
No problem.

33
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:11,130
So are we friends again?

34
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,670
- Yeah.     - Okay.

35
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:17,260
Ahem. You won't believe what Monica's brother just said to me!

36
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:58,550
What you doing, Mon?

37
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,800
I'm listing all the things that could go wrong at the wedding.

38
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,260
So I can be prepared.

39
00:03:06,510 --> 00:03:10,890
- Mm-hm. What are they?     - "The dresses won't get picked up...

40
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:14,560
...veil gets lost, and I'm missing something blue."

41
00:03:14,810 --> 00:03:16,860
Those are all the things I'm responsible for.

42
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,240
I had to go with the odds.

43
00:03:21,450 --> 00:03:22,820
Hey! You guys!

44
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:25,490
Remember I had that audition a while ago, and I didn't get that part?

45
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:26,740
- The commercial?     - No.

46
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:27,910
- That play?     - No.

47
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,370
- That other play?     - No.

48
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,660
- The movie?     - Yes!

49
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:35,290
- The one about the pilot and his dog?     - No.

50
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,710
But man, that one hurt.

51
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:42,090
- This is the one about WWI soldiers.     - Oh, yeah.

52
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:45,090
Back then we called it "The Great War."

53
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:48,350
It really was.

54
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:53,270
A guy they wanted backed out and now they want me! I start shooting today!

55
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,650
Congratulations!

56
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:58,320
- Today's the rehearsal dinner.     - I'll be done by then.

57
00:03:58,570 --> 00:04:01,280
Oh. Then way to go, you big movie star!

58
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:04,240
See you. I'm off to fight the Nazis.

59
00:04:04,490 --> 00:04:08,830
Wait, Joey. We fought the Nazis in WWll, not WWI.

60
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,080
Whoa. Okay.

61
00:04:11,410 --> 00:04:13,210
Who was in WWI?

62
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,750
Go ahead.

63
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:21,210
- You're gonna be late! Go! Go!     - Yeah, I'll see you.

64
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:25,680
Who did we fight in WWI?

65
00:04:25,970 --> 00:04:28,470
- Mexico?     - Yes. Very good.

66
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:33,090

67
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,240
- Hey, Joey. We're ready.     - Yeah, me too.

68
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:49,530
Richard, we're ready for you.

69
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:53,410
Joey Tribbiani, Richard Crosby is playing Vincent.

70
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:57,460
- I'm doing my scenes with you?     - Nice to meet you.

71
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:01,840
I can't believe this. Incredible. You just won an Oscar.

72
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:04,260
No, I didn't.

73
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:06,550
I think you did.

74
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,760
I think I lost, three times.

75
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:14,680
- Uh, cookie? Would you?     - No.

76
00:05:15,390 --> 00:05:19,400
Okay. We're about an hour away from getting the scene lit.

77
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:23,860
- So, uh, can you guys run it a couple times?     - Yeah, sure.

78
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:25,940
All right. Let's do it.

79
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,700
And action!

80
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:34,040
- We have to find the platoon!     - Forget the platoon. The platoon is gone!

81
00:05:37,250 --> 00:05:41,380
- What?     - The platoon's dead! Face facts, Tony!

82
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:46,210
What'll we do? We have no reinforcements or food.

83
00:05:46,470 --> 00:05:50,220
There's food in the basement. Potatoes and some pasta.

84
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:54,770
Hang on. Joey, you keep touching your face.

85
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:56,100
Something wrong?

86
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,770
No.

87
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:00,350
I, uh...

88
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:03,570
I thought it might be a cool character thing.

89
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:06,610
He's a face toucher.

90
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,740
I don't think so.

91
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:17,200
Let's take it back to Richard's last lines. Action!

92
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,580
We may not have any weapons, but we still have food.

93
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:22,580
Potatoes, pasta...

94
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,750
...and a few tins of tuna!

95
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:29,930
- Honey, we gotta go!     - Okay.

96
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:32,300
Here's a question you never want to ask:

97
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:36,430
My dad just called and wants to know if he can borrow one of your pearl necklaces?

98
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:39,980
Did he say what kind of neckline he's wearing?

99
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:41,980
No.

100
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:46,270
I've only met him once but I'm guessing, plunging?

101
00:06:46,530 --> 00:06:51,200
He is more of a "If you've got it, flaunt it" kind of father.

102
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,570
I don't have anything but let me see if Rachel does.

103
00:06:54,830 --> 00:06:56,870
Yes, include more people in this.

104
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:02,920
Hey. Do you realize that tomorrow we're gonna be getting married?

105
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:05,210
I have a date tomorrow night.

106
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:10,720
- I can't believe we made it.     - You don't have to sound so surprised.

107
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:12,430
I'm sorry, but...

108
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:15,800
- Nothing.     - What?

109
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:20,390
Well, honestly? Ever since we got engaged...

110
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:23,440
...I've waited for you to flip out.

111
00:07:23,690 --> 00:07:26,230
Honestly? Me too.

112
00:07:27,070 --> 00:07:28,570
- Really?     - Yeah.

113
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:32,240
I think that something stupid will come up and I'll...

114
00:07:33,030 --> 00:07:34,320
...go all Chandler.

115
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:37,490
- But nothing has.     - I'm so glad.

116
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:40,500
Thank you for staying so calm during this.

117
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,960
It's made me stay calm.

118
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:46,210
- I could've been worse.     - Okay.

119
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,420
I'll be right there.

120
00:07:55,090 --> 00:07:57,470
Hi, if you're calling before Saturday...

121
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:59,180
...you've reached Monica and Chandler.

122
00:07:59,350 --> 00:08:03,810
But if you're calling after Saturday, you've reached Mr. And Mrs. Bing.

123
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:07,270
Please leave a message for the Bings!

124
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:25,830
- Maureen!     - Hi.

125
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:30,630
- Gosh. This is my cousin, Maureen.     - We're the Bings.

126
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,590
Hi! You guys look so beautiful.

127
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,550
Mr. And Mrs. Bing!

128
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:43,560
Wow, Monica.

129
00:08:43,810 --> 00:08:47,600
So you know, I had my older-brother talk with Chandler.

130
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,650
- What is that?     - Well, I...

131
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,530
I told him that if he ever hurt you...

132
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:56,610
...I would hunt him down and kick his ass.

133
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:02,950
What is the matter with everybody? I'm serious.

134
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,460
I would kick his ass!

135
00:09:07,290 --> 00:09:10,340
Ross, please, my makeup!

136
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:13,210
Hi.

137
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:14,970
- Chandler.     - Mom.

138
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,760
Thanks for wearing... something.

139
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:24,890
Ohh. This is so exciting! I thought we screwed you up too much for this.

140
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:31,060
Just think, soon there will be lots of little Bings.

141
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:39,320
I can't believe I have to go back to work after this and get spit on again.

142
00:09:39,570 --> 00:09:42,990
You're lucky. At least the people who spit on you are famous.

143
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:47,330
- Who spits on you?     - I don't wanna talk about work.

144
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:53,590
Mrs. Bing? These are my parents, Judy and Jack Geller.

145
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:57,630
- It's lovely to meet you.     - Are you his mother or father?

146
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:59,590
Jack!

147
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:03,180
What? I've never seen one before.

148
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:05,720
Dad, there's Ross. Go talk to him.

149
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:09,190
I didn't even have a chance to act as if I'm okay with it.

150
00:10:12,270 --> 00:10:14,480
Hello, all.

151
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,530
Hi... Dad.

152
00:10:19,490 --> 00:10:21,360
Hi, Mr. Bing.

153
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,950
- Nora.     - Charles.

154
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:30,580
- It's so great to see you both here.     - Yes.

155
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:34,500
Although we may be seeing too much of some people.

156
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:40,550
Aren't you too old to wear a dress like that?

157
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:44,930
Don't you have too much penis to wear a dress like that?

158
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:48,350
Oh, my God.

159
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:53,690
Of course you can kick his ass, son.

160
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:57,440
You could kick anyone's ass you want to.

161
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,990
Thanks, you guys.

162
00:11:04,410 --> 00:11:05,740
- Rach, Rach?     - Yeah?

163
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:10,000
Do me a favor. Talk to Chandler's dad and keep him away from Chandler's mom.

164
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:14,540
- Yeah, but I don't know what he looks like.     - He is the man in a black dress.

165
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:25,640
Hi. I'm Rachel, a friend of Monica and Chandler's.

166
00:11:25,850 --> 00:11:28,970
- I'm Amanda.      - Oh, I get it.

167
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:32,480
"A man, duh!"

168
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:39,230
Could I have your attention?

169
00:11:40,190 --> 00:11:44,570
- I'm Ross Geller.     - Dr. Ross Geller.

170
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:49,580
Dad, please. As I was saying...

171
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:52,500
...I'm Dr. Ross Geller.

172
00:11:53,370 --> 00:11:55,880
Uh, and I'm the best man.

173
00:11:56,040 --> 00:12:00,510
And this marriage is doubly special for me...

174
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:04,840
...um, because not only is the groom my best friend...

175
00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:09,600
...but, uh, the bride is my little sister.

176
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:14,100
She's the greatest sister a guy could ask for.

177
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:18,360
Please join me in raising a glass...

178
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:22,440
...to the couple we're here to celebrate.

179
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:26,070
- To the Bings.     - To the Bings!

180
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,290
I'm gonna steam my dress.

181
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:39,290
Who will make sure nothing happens to it?

182
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,300
- I'll do it.     - Who wants it? Anybody?

183
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,220
- I said I'll do it.     - Nobody?

184
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:49,510
- All right, I'll do it myself.     - I'm not gonna screw it up.

185
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:53,350
You're right. I'm sorry. You were a big help tonight.

186
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:57,190
And thanks for putting my grandmother in the cab to get to the hotel.

187
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:00,480
- Of course! That's what I'm here for.     - Okay. Sorry.

188
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:03,070
Ugh! Pssh.

189
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:05,030
What grandmother?

190
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:12,830
- Where have you been?     - Taking my parents to the hotel.

191
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,160
- Going back to work?     - Yeah.

192
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:19,000
- Nice shades.     - If I wear these in my scenes...

193
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:21,630
...I won't get spit in my eyes.

194
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:27,760
And, if I remember correctly, Ray-Ban was the official sponsor of WWI.

195
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:31,350
Great! All right!

196
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,470
- I'll see you later.     - All right.

197
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:37,060
- Where's Chandler?      - I think he's in Rachel's room. See you.

198
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:46,240
Chandler?

199
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:04,300
- Hey.      - Hi.

200
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:07,720
- Is Monica here?      - She's steaming her dress. Why?

201
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:11,550
- I think Chandler's gone.     - What?

202
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:16,430
- He left that.      - "Tell Monica I'm sorry."

203
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,060
Oh, my God.

204
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,100
What's up?

205
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:25,530
"Tell Monica I'm sorry."

206
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,860
Tell her yourself.

207
00:14:35,290 --> 00:14:38,330
Oh, my God. Chandler just left, though?

208
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:41,170
Maybe it's not what we think. Maybe it's:

209
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:45,210
"Tell Monica I'm sorry I drank the last of the milk."

210
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:51,090
Or maybe he was writing to tell her that he's changed his name:

211
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:54,050
"Tell Monica, I'm Sorry."

212
00:14:56,020 --> 00:15:01,060
- It means he freaked out and left!      - Don't be so negative!

213
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:06,900
Good God, isn't it possible that "Sorry" is sitting in there right now?

214
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:12,030
Phoebe, I think Ross is right. What are we gonna do?

215
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:15,870
I'm gonna have to go find him and bring him back.

216
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,700
You make sure Monica does not find out, okay?

217
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:23,080
But, if you don't find him and bring him back...

218
00:15:23,330 --> 00:15:27,420
...I am gonna hunt you down and kick your ass!

219
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:31,170
I will find him.

220
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:37,720
Joey? Can you go through these lines with me?

221
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:40,980
Oh, man, they just re-did my makeup.

222
00:15:42,310 --> 00:15:45,560
- Just the last two pages.      - All right.

223
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,610
I found the picture!

224
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:54,740
Picture? What picture?

225
00:15:54,990 --> 00:15:58,080
The picture of my wife! I found it in your pack!

226
00:15:58,370 --> 00:16:00,410
Could you lower the script?

227
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:02,870
I don't want to.

228
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:07,340
I need to see your face so I can play off your reaction.

229
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:09,960
Okay, look.

230
00:16:10,170 --> 00:16:14,930
I know you're great and play all those Shakespeare guys...

231
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,720
...but you're spitting all over me, man.

232
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:21,560
- Of course I am!      - You know you've been spitting?

233
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:24,060
That's what real actors do.

234
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:28,730
Enunciation is the mark of a good actor.

235
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:32,190
And when you enunciate, you spit!

236
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,910
Wow. Didn't know that.

237
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,080
Thanks. Okay, check it out.

238
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,870
Picture? What picture?

239
00:16:52,630 --> 00:16:56,380
- Have you seen Chandler?     - No, I haven't seen him.

240
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,680
- Damn.      - He's getting married tomorrow, right?

241
00:16:59,930 --> 00:17:02,640
Yes. Don't worry. Everything's fine.

242
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:06,190
- See you at the wedding.      - I wasn't invited.

243
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:11,190
Then we'll see you the day after tomorrow.

244
00:17:14,190 --> 00:17:15,650
Mom? Dad?

245
00:17:16,490 --> 00:17:18,200
What are you doing here?

246
00:17:18,450 --> 00:17:21,910
You kids talk about this place so much, we thought we'd see what the fuss is all about.

247
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:25,830
- I see why the girls like coming here.      - Why?

248
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:28,790
The sexy blond behind the counter.

249
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:38,380
- Gunther?      - She just added him to her list.

250
00:17:39,390 --> 00:17:43,100
- Your list?     - Of people we're allowed to sleep...

251
00:17:43,390 --> 00:17:45,930
I know what the list is.

252
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,730
Sit down, have a cup of joe.

253
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,480
I can't, I'm sorry.

254
00:17:52,730 --> 00:17:56,150
If you see Chandler, tell him I'm looking for him.

255
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:59,860
And if you see Rita Moreno, let her know I'm looking for her.

256
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,580
Action!

257
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,790
I found the picture!

258
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:15,420
What picture?

259
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:19,590
A picture of my wife, in your pack!

260
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,930
You went through my personal property?

261
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:27,810
Why do you have a picture of Paulette in your pack?

262
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:34,400
Because, Vincent, we were lovers...

263
00:18:35,530 --> 00:18:37,530
...for two years!

264
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:40,450
Cut! Wonderful!

265
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:44,700
Great scene, huh?

266
00:18:44,950 --> 00:18:48,580
You were awesome. In that last speech, you soaked me.

267
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:52,250
- Tomorrow's call sheet.     - I'm not working tomorrow.

268
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:55,550
- You are now.      - No, you gotta get me out of it.

269
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:58,050
I have plans. Important plans!

270
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:10,180
- Still no word from Chandler.      - Oh, man.

271
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:13,810
But they found the grandmother wandering down 5th.

272
00:19:15,150 --> 00:19:17,360
Okay, well there's one down.

273
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:20,700
I'm getting married today!

274
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:28,200
I cracked a rib, but I don't care. Today's my wedding!

275
00:19:28,410 --> 00:19:30,960
My day is finally here!

276
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:36,340
She might not even notice he's gone.

277
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,300
I'm gonna start getting ready!

278
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:46,140
We can't let her start getting ready. This is too awful!

279
00:19:46,350 --> 00:19:49,470
She'll be in the gown, and he won't show up.

280
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:52,600
Then she'll have to take off the gown...

281
00:19:52,810 --> 00:19:55,480
Stop it. You can't do this here.

282
00:19:57,110 --> 00:19:58,610
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

283
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:01,320
It's just so sad.

284
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,570
Pull it together. She can't see you like this.

285
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:07,990
- She'll know something's wrong.     - I know. I know.

286
00:20:08,870 --> 00:20:10,490
There's no tissue.

287
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:13,210
Can you grab me some toilet paper?

288
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:17,380
Oh, that's gone too. This is Monica's bathroom, right?

289
00:20:18,130 --> 00:20:20,710
- I found one.      - Okay.

290
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:25,300
Thank you.

291
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:27,390
Oh, God.

292
00:20:29,810 --> 00:20:31,770
Can I have another one?

293
00:20:32,810 --> 00:20:34,230
Sure.

294
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,270
Do you need some floss?

295
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:44,700
I can't imagine what will happen if he doesn't show up.

296
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:46,450
Here's a whole bunch.

297
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,870
She'll be at the wedding waiting...

298
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:52,620
...and people will be whispering, "That poor girl."

299
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:56,210
Then she'll have to come back here and live alone.

300
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,290
- Oh, my God.      - What?

301
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:03,970
There was a pregnancy test in the garbage, and it's positive.

302
00:21:04,590 --> 00:21:06,680
Monica's pregnant.

303
00:21:08,890 --> 00:21:11,680
So I guess she won't be totally alone.

304
00:21:18,310 --> 00:21:19,520
Next time on Friends:

305
00:21:19,690 --> 00:21:22,440
- We've gotta tell her that he's gone.      - No, we can't.

306
00:21:22,610 --> 00:21:24,280
She's gonna start getting ready soon.

307
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,450
Can't you stall her a little?

308
00:21:26,610 --> 00:21:28,700
I'm never gonna get married.

309
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:34,950
We've just got one short scene. It's just you and Richard, and he's a pro.

310
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:38,040
- Are you drunk?     - No!

311
00:21:38,210 --> 00:21:40,880
- Yes, you are!     - All right.

312
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:44,210
- How's Chandler?      - Great!

313
00:21:44,380 --> 00:21:45,970
- Where are you?     - On the set.

314
00:21:46,130 --> 00:21:48,800
This is turning into the worst wedding day ever.

